# The server this release line tests against. compose.yml deliberately declares no defaults, so
# that a stack can never silently bring up the wrong ELN; this file is where the 400.x line
# supplies them. The 312.x line ships its own values — see README.md for both.
#
# IMAGES ARE PINNED BY DIGEST ON PURPOSE. Bumping a digest is a deliberate, reviewed change:
# record the new digest together with the `Version:` string that /about then reports.
#
# Pinned 2026-11-11 — ELN v4.0.1, the first immutable v4 release images:
#   eln  complat/chemotion:eln-4.0.1
#   db   complat/chemotion:db-4.0.1
#
# Two things changed with this bump, and both are the point of it:
#
# 1. The publisher moved. Release images are now `complat/chemotion`, not `ptrxyz/chemotion`
#    (which stops at 3.1.2, May 2026) and not `complat/chemotion_eln_stage` either.
# 2. A real release tag exists at last. Until 2026-11-10 the only v4 image was the rolling
#    `next-release`, rebuilt whenever the v4 branch moved — which is why this file pinned a
#    digest of it and why CHANGELOG.md had to say v4 alignment was reached "by source
#    inspection, not by a live run". That sentence can now be a measured claim.
#
# Superseded pins, kept so a bisect can reproduce an older run:
#   2026-08-21  eln  complat/chemotion_eln_stage:next-release@sha256:3520ac2cf46301f53eddf68b58971ca74ca8a2dd331c96765cad02c13b021343  (v4.0.0-rc-260818)
#   2026-08-21  db   complat/dev:postgres16-rdkit@sha256:326d2ef0ee96cc7a8da7569a1637b1527abaa9cd0c1c680b7320223febfd254c
CHEMOTION_ELN_IMAGE=complat/chemotion:eln-4.0.1@sha256:5777517ab5e526aa3699b77e12086a726575a77d6742a61b114505932883ca3d
CHEMOTION_DB_IMAGE=complat/chemotion:db-4.0.1@sha256:780e0d574fb4c8334cf383cfe674e899cb0265ad68fdc829590baf0b20613435

# Keeps this line's volumes apart from the other line's, which survive `docker compose down`.
CHEMOTION_STACK_SUFFIX=v4
